#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""tasks: the command line for the hub's task list (http://beacon), for agents and for him.

  tasks                              open tasks, most urgent first (same as `tasks ls`)
  tasks ls [-p PROJECT] [--claude] [--due today] [--stale] [-q TEXT] [--parked] [--all] [--json]
  tasks add "Title" [-b BODY|-b -] [-p PROJECT] [--priority 1-4] [--due 2026-10-07[T14:00]] [-t TAG]... [--doing]
  tasks show ID          tasks done ID [-m NOTE]     tasks drop ID [-m NOTE]
  tasks doing ID         tasks todo ID               tasks note ID "text" (or - for stdin)
  tasks set ID priority=2 due=2026-10-08 project=x tags=claude,marketing title="..."
  tasks link ID [SESSION_ID]         tasks auth (is the token good?)
  tasks handoff ID "what is left"    left for the task agent: noted, back to todo with his go-ahead (claude)
                                     unless it is an agent's own idea (auto), which still waits for his OK

Decisions for him (http://beacon/decisions), so an agent never stops a turn to ask:
  tasks ask (or tasks decide) "Question?" -o "your pick" -o "other" [-k KIND] [-c CONTEXT|-c -] [--blocking] [--task ID]
  tasks wait ID [ID...] [--timeout SECONDS]   only while he is chatting live (10 min at most); else end your turn
  tasks questions [--answered|--all] [-k KIND] [--since DAYS] [--kinds] [--json]
  tasks answer ID "text" [-m NOTE] [--always] [--chat]   tasks withdraw ID [-m WHY]
  (--chat: he answered in your own chat. Log it that way, never withdraw a question he answered.)
  tasks block ID   you hold the work until he answers after all: the same card turns blocking (never ask twice)

A task filed from inside a Claude Code session is linked to that session, so the hub can tell
when everything the session asked for is done. The project defaults to the git repo you are in,
else "personal". Writes use TASKS_TOKEN (env, else `secrets get TASKS_TOKEN`); the hub is
TASKS_URL (default http://beacon). Standard library only.
"""
