# ------------------------------------------------------------ approval gate (task 1764)
# Two layers keep an agent from sending, paying, publishing, deleting, going live or reaching other
# people on its own default. Both use the code below, and so does the hub (hub/gate.py loads this
# file), so a question and an action are judged by the same words. Deterministic: no model here.
#   Layer 1, the hub: every question blocks unless its kind is on LOW_RISK_KINDS and its text hits
#     no RISK_TEXT word. The agent's --blocking can raise that, never lower it.
#   Layer 2, `tasks hook-gate` (a global PreToolUse hook): a risky tool call (RISK_CALLS) passes only
#     with his yes: his own words in this chat, or a question he answered on the page or a task.
#     GATE_MODE (~/.claude/gate-mode, else shadow) decides: shadow only logs, enforce denies.
# Kept above the heavy imports: the hook runs before every Bash and MCP call (~40 ms).

def fold(text):
    """Lowercase without accents: 'Pošli' and 'posli' are one word."""
    return ''.join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', str(text or '').casefold())
                   if not unicodedata.combining(c))


